## 5. Things in the reviews I believe are wrong (not applied)
- a#39 suggested "כגון ישראל וטאיוואן" and a#40 suggested contrasting Israeli
  פיצויי פיטורים. Both would assert the law of the reader's country, which the
  rulebook forbids and which the checker's `nationality` list for he
  ('ישראל', 'ישראלי', 'אזרחות ישראלית') blocks outright. Applied as R2 neutral instead.
- a#36 / a#47 / b#29 ask for the Korean-blog one-sentence-per-line layout to be
  restored to a normal register. Merging or splitting blocks breaks the `blocks`
  parity gate and the WO's hard rule, so only the wording inside each block was fixed.
- a#5 reads טאיצ׳ונג's practice as "Bausachen" (construction). I applied
  "ענייני בנייה", but flag it: the English canonical says "engineering and
  construction matters" — if the firm means engineering, revert to "ענייני הנדסה".
- b#40 suggested "ירושה בדרך של החלפה" for 代位繼承. Israeli law would say
  "ירושה מכוח ייצוג / חליפין"; I used the reviewer's wording for consistency with the
  Chinese gloss, but an attorney review may prefer "ירושה מכוח ייצוג (代位繼承)".

